examples.question_text:
For $f(x)=x^2-8x+13$, find the coordinates of the points where the tangent:
(a) is horizontal;
(b) has gradient $4$.

examples.solution_text:
Write the line in gradient-intercept form.
$\begin{aligned}3x-y+2&=0\\y&=3x+2\end{aligned}$
Parallel lines have the same gradient, so the required tangent gradient is $3$.

$\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=4x-5\\4x-5&=3\\4x&=8\\x&=2\\f(2)&=2(2)^2-5(2)+4\\&=2\end{aligned}$
The point is $(2,2)$.

The red tangent has the same gradient as the green given line.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{tangentred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{linegreen}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\draw[->,black] (-0.4,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-4.4)--(0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,domain=-0.15:2.7,samples=70,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2*\x*\x-5*\x+4});
\draw[tangentred,thick,domain=0.2:3,samples=2,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x-4});
\draw[linegreen,thick,domain=-0.3:1,samples=2,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x+2});
\fill[black] (2,2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,2) node[right] {$(2,2)$};
\path (0.55,3.65) node[left] {$y=3x+2$};
\path (1,-1) node[right] {$y=3x-4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
